cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ECOCIDE: A Satellite-Based Evidentiary Framework for War-Time Environmental Crimes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Maske"
    given-names: "Sakshi D."
repository-code: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
url: "https://github.com/sakshimaske303-commits/ECOCIDE"
abstract: >-
  A causal-inference framework applying Difference-in-Differences analysis,
  placebo testing, and quarterly event-study validation to independently
  quantify conflict-attributable environmental damage from the destruction
  of Ukraine's Kakhovka Dam (6 June 2023). Comparing monthly NDVI in the
  conflict-affected Kherson Oblast against a matched non-conflict control
  zone (Tulcea County, Romania), the analysis identifies a statistically
  significant vegetation decline attributable to the event, validated
  through placebo testing and HAC-robust standard errors, alongside a
  verified multi-sensor UNOSAT flood-extent timeline. The project is
  designed to fill a specific, acknowledged gap in existing satellite-based
  assessments of environmental war damage, which rely on qualitative
  interpretation and explicitly decline to establish statistical causality.
keywords:
  - ecocide
  - remote sensing
  - causal inference
  - difference-in-differences
  - war crimes
  - satellite evidence
  - Kakhovka Dam
  - NDVI
  - geospatial analysis
